The AI explores by sea: it never built a boat. ChooseProducible let a sea unit through only when the unit would get an ExplorerAI (a check that also added a phantom exploration target every time it was scored) and then gave it no value, so a Curragh scored about 7 against an Archer's 19 and was never built; in six 200-turn Continents and Archipelago games no AI built one. A coastal city now builds a ship while the ocean next to it has unknown tiles bordering what its civ knows (ExplorerAI.HasOceanToExplore, which changes nothing), the civ is at peace, and the civ's ships, built or being built, number fewer than min(4, 1 + cities / 6); such a ship gets +15, which the cheap Curragh wins. ExplorerAI also took an unreachable target for a reachable one (no route gives an empty path of length 0, not null) and let a ship pick targets on any water: a boat on a lake accepted explore and never moved. A ship now explores only the body of water it is on, or in port those next to it, and an unreachable target is skipped.

